## Why This Is Asked

Tests handling of cross-region, multi-tenant telemetry with data quality gates and runtime policy enforcement, requiring the candidate to design a robust data lineage, idempotence, and schema evolution using DVA primitives.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant isolation with Kinesis Streams and DynamoDB catalog
- Glue Schema Registry for backward/forward compatibility
- Runtime data quality checks and DLQ handling
- Idempotent writes and cross-region S3 replication
- OpenTelemetry tracing across services

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent write to DynamoDB
async function idempotentWrite(event, db) {
  const key = event.deviceId + '|' + event.ts;
  await db.put({
    TableName: 'idempotency',
    Item: { key, ts: event.ts },
    ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(key)'
  }).promise();
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce per-tenant retention vs. cost controls?
- How would you monitor SLA and detect drift in the pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate policy-driven data masking with AWS DVA components, ensure regional data residency, and preserve auditability while maintaining low latency.

## Key Concepts

- Ingestion-time masking and policy evaluation
- EU data residency, per-tenant masking rules
- Policy engine integration (OPA) with Lambda/Fargate workflows
- Immutable audit trails (S3 Object Lock, DynamoDB logs)

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskPII(record, fields) {
  const out = {...record};
  fields.forEach(f => {
    if (typeof out[f] === 'string') {
      const v = out[f];
      out[f] = v.replace(/.(?=.{4})/g, '*');
    }
  });
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that EU masking rules are enforced without impacting non-EU tenants, and how would you test the policy at scale?
- What tracing and audit mechanisms would you implement to ensure data lineage and integrity after masking, including replay considerations?

